          "stageRecord": "Project CP above the established IP. Move the finite auxiliary from I to C, leaving a head trace, and move Boken from the already established Spec-IP position to Spec-CP, leaving a subject trace. These operations implement a uniform CP analysis of Swedish root V2 clauses: the initial constituent occupies Spec-CP and the finite verb occupies C. Subject fronting here does not require a contrastive-topic interpretation. The auxiliary moves to the next higher head without skipping an intervening head. The nominal dependency passes through the Case position in Spec-IP rather than moving directly from the object position to Spec-CP. Its A-chain segment receives the Theme role at the object trace and nominative at the subject position; its upper A′ segment is locally antecedent-governed by the fronted NP. The finite-head chain preserves the licensing properties of I. No Principle A or B configuration is introduced, and neither referential NP is illicitly bound under Principle C. The completed sentence is grammatical: it describes the book undergoing a reading event with Sara as Agent. The passive bli construction is not analyzed as a copular adjective with an unrelated PP. The pronounced terminals reproduce all five supplied tokens in order.",
          "statement": "Complete the grammatical Swedish root declarative with subject-first V2 structure.",
